file: Write a file, or set the owner, group, and mode of a file.

Keys:
  path       string      required  The absolute path of the file.
  content    string      -         The content of the file, as a string.
  template   string      -         A template in the recipe's templates directory.
  source     string      -         A file in the recipe's files directory.
  copy_from  string      -         A file on the host to copy the content from.
  stock      boolean     false     Write the content that the installed package ships for path.
  owner      name or ID  root      The owner of the file, a user name or a numeric ID.
  group      name or ID  root      The group of the file, a group name or a numeric ID.
  mode       string      0644      The mode of the file, in octal, such as 0640.
  validate   string      -         A command that checks the new file.
  absent     boolean     false     Remove the file.
  replace    boolean     false     Remove another kind of thing at path first, such as a directory.

Example:
  - name: Write the message of the day
    file:
      path: /etc/motd
      content: "Welcome to mail.example.com.\n"
      mode: "0644"

Run "winch doc file.<key>" for the full text of a key.
